question: >
  On enforcement locus — where a constraint actually lives and gets checked:
  declared in the schema/contract, or asserted by a script or test at run time —
  the records assert both schema declared constraint (3 judgments, 0 authored)
  and runtime check (3 judgments, 1 authored). Which should be the stated rule,
  and where is the exception?

why_it_matters: >
  Until this is answered, a record below Dave inherits whichever side it happens
  to copy. Full draft pending: the proposal batch for this axis did not
  complete; the axis, poles, counts and evidence are real, the options below are
  the generic form.

